Commands

DATABASE > CREATE DATABASE your_database; > Creates a database within SQL 

TABLE > CREATE TABLE your_table (data columns); > Creates a table within the current database 

INSERT > INSERT INTO your_database(data types) > Inserts data into a table 

VALUES > VALUES (numberdata,'your_data'), ('more_data'); > This is how you select what data is added to your table

SELECT > SELECT 'desired_data' FROM 'your_table'; > Used to view data within a table

ORDER BY > ORDER BY 'data_type'; > This displays your data within the table in order by ascending 

DISTICT > SELECT DISTINCT 'data_type' FROM 'your_table'; > Searches for unique data within your table 

WHERE > SELECT 'data' FROM 'table' WHERE 'data_type' = 'your_data' > Gathers data from a specific data type

BETWEEN > SELECT 'data_type FROM 'your_table' WHERE 'data_type' BETWEEN 'value' AND 'value' > Gathers all data within a range

AND > SELECT 'data_type FROM 'your_table' WHERE 'data_type' BETWEEN 'value' AND 'value' > To select multiple types of data

LIKE > SELECT 'data_type FROM 'your_table' WHERE 'data_type' LIKE 'value%' > Find data similar to what is inputed

OR > SELECT 'data_type FROM 'your_table' WHERE 'data_type' = 'value' OR 'data_type' = 'value'



Data Types 

varchar(amount) > Characters and how many allowed  

date > Must input a date in the format year-month-day 

numeric > Must input a number 

BIGSERIAL > Gives an id number to each data input automaticaly 



Syntax

; > SQL must end with a semicolon (;)

* > This is used to select all items within the code

DESC > This is how you change the order that "ORDER BY" gives you from ascending to descending

= > Equal to

<> > Not equal 

> > Greater than 

< > Less than 

>= > Greater than equal to

<= > Less than equal to

IN: > match one of several values

'YYYY-MM-DD' > Is how you input a date

% > Wild card so and number of characters can appear 

_ > used to match one unknown character 

() > Used to combine multiple data types or commands together

